Shared readout
--------------
1. 2D Haar packets multiply by coordinatewise interval meet/refinement.
2. Fixed-path tournament tilings multiply by symmetric difference of
   staircase tile supports, the Boolean Haar/Walsh product rule.
3. Both algebras are exact before quotienting and lossy after strip/count
   scalarization unless owner coordinates are retained.
4. LRC14 discrepancy should therefore be carried by labelled packets:
   q/Farey scale, Haar open/boundary state, endpoint owners, packet family,
   and certificate handoff.  AP/GW are boundary packets, not scalar zeros.

