Candidate theorem target
------------------------
A quotient used in the LRC14 proof must be a homomorphism for the relevant
Haar/Walsh packet product, or it must emit a named residual coefficient.
Equivalently: scalar discrepancy, strip counts, and tournament isomorphism
classes are admissible only after the lost 2D tile/rectangle address is
reconstructed, annihilated by orthogonality, or routed to a state-lift/F7
residual packet.
